## Engineering Notes

### Engineering Observations

SO-F-001 serves as the foundational functional objective for the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

All future Functional Objectives shall refine, support, or extend the capability established by this objective while remaining traceable to it.

---

### Engineering Considerations

As the objective library expands, this objective should remain stable.

Future engineering effort should focus on deriving specialized child objectives rather than modifying the root objective unless a fundamental change to the AVIA mission is formally approved.

---

### Known Limitations

This objective intentionally defines the highest-level functional capability.

It does not specify:

- System architecture
- Hardware or software implementation
- Algorithms
- Interfaces
- Performance targets
- Safety constraints

These shall be defined by derived objectives and their associated engineering artifacts.

---

### Future Considerations

Future Functional Objectives are expected to elaborate this objective through capabilities such as:

- Environmental perception
- Context interpretation
- Adaptive decision generation
- Approved action execution
- Learning and adaptation
- Human collaboration and authority management

---

### Engineering Note

SO-F-001 should be regarded as a stable engineering anchor for the Functional Objective hierarchy.

Changes to this objective should occur only when the fundamental mission of AVIA changes, as such changes may propagate throughout the entire engineering repository.
